    <div class="bb-card">
        <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> Generated members, by declaration</h3>
        <p>What the generator adds to your partial class, for each thing you declare.</p>
        <div class="bb-scroll">
            <table class="bb-table">
                <thead><tr><th>You declare</th><th>Generated</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>[BlexStore]</code> on <code>partial class Foo</code></td>
                        <td>
                            <code>partial class Foo : BlexStoreBase</code>,
                            <code>override string Name =&gt; base.WithInstanceKey("foo")</code> (the declared name, plus <code>:{key}</code> for a scoped instance),
                            <code>override JsonObject SerializeState()</code>,
                            <code>override void DeserializeState(JsonObject)</code>,
                            and <code>override DescribeActions()</code> listing the store's action descriptors - its actions and effects, plus a <code>"Set Foo"</code> per state property
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>[BlexStore(Persist = true)]</code></td>
                        <td><code>override bool Persist =&gt; true</code></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>[BlexStore(EnforceActions = true)]</code></td>
                        <td>every state setter is <code>private set</code>, <code>override bool EnforcesActions =&gt; true</code>, and no <code>"Set Foo"</code> descriptors</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>[BlexState] private T _foo;</code></td>
                        <td><code>public T Foo { get; set; }</code> - the setter routes through <code>SetState</code>; the field is included in both snapshot methods</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>[BlexState(Persist = false)] private T _foo;</code></td>
                        <td>the same property, and <code>"Foo"</code> in an <code>override TransientStateKeys</code> - kept out of durable persistence</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>[BlexComputed] T ComputeFoo()</code></td>
                        <td><code>public T Foo { get; }</code> plus <code>__FooValid</code> / <code>__FooValue</code>, and an entry in <code>InvalidateComputed()</code></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>[BlexAction] void OnFoo(A a)</code></td>
                        <td><code>public void Foo(A a)</code></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>[BlexAction] Task OnFoo(A a)</code></td>
                        <td><code>public Task Foo(A a)</code></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>[BlexEffect] Task OnFoo(A a)</code></td>
                        <td>
                            <code>public Task Foo(A a)</code>,
                            <code>public bool FooIsLoading</code>,
                            <code>public Exception? FooError</code>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>[BlexEffect] Task OnFoo(A a, CancellationToken ct)</code></td>
                        <td>the above, plus <code>public void CancelFoo()</code> - and note the token is <em>not</em> on the public signature</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>any <code>[BlexAction]</code> or <code>[BlexEffect]</code></td>
                        <td>
                            a field in the nested <code>public static class Actions</code>:
                            <code>BlexAction&lt;Foo&gt; Bar</code> for <code>OnBar()</code>,
                            <code>BlexAction&lt;Foo, A&gt; Bar</code> for <code>OnBar(A a)</code>,
                            <code>BlexAction&lt;Foo, (A A, B B)&gt; Bar</code> for <code>OnBar(A a, B b)</code>.
                            Not generated - with warning <code>BLEX020</code> - when the store already has a member named <code>Actions</code>.
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bb-card">
        <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> Reserved names</h3>
        <p>
            A generated member may not take one of these - they are inherited from <code>BlexStoreBase</code>
            or emitted by the generator itself. Collisions are reported as <code>BLEX005</code>. The name
            <code>Actions</code> is different: taking it costs only the typed descriptors (<code>BLEX020</code>).
        </p>
        <CodeBlock Code="@Reserved" Language="text" Title="Reserved" />
    </div>

    <div class="bb-card">
        <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-warning"></span> JSON conventions</h3>
        <p>
            Snapshots use <code>BlexJson.Options</code>: <code>JsonSerializerDefaults.Web</code>,
            case-insensitive property matching and enums written as strings. Slices are keyed by the
            generated <em>property</em> name (<code>Count</code>, not <code>_count</code>), and the global
            tree is keyed by store name.
        </p>
        <CodeBlock Code="@JsonShape" Language="json" />
    </div>

